# StoryVerse Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode)
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Auth: Supabase Auth
- State: Zustand + TanStack Query
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Testing: Vitest, React Testing Library

## Code Style

### Imports
- Use absolute imports with @/ prefix
- Order: React → Next.js → External → Internal → Types → Styles

### Components
- Functional components only
- Props interface above component
- Export named functions (not default)

```tsx
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string
  onClick?: () => void
}

export function Component({ title, onClick }: ComponentProps) {
  return <div onClick={onClick}>{title}</div>
}
```

### API Routes
```tsx
import { NextRequest } from 'next/server'
import { apiSuccess, apiError } from '@/lib/api-response'

export async function GET(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const data = await fetchData()
    return apiSuccess(data)
  } catch (error) {
    return apiError('Error message', 500)
  }
}
```

## UI Components

### Always use existing components:
- Button: `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`
  - Variants: default, outline, ghost, destructive
  - Sizes: default, sm, lg
- Card: `import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from "@/components/ui/card"`
- Input: `import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input"`
- Badge: `import { Badge } from "@/components/ui/badge"`
- Modal: `import { Modal } from "@/components/ui/modal"`
- Skeleton: `import { Skeleton } from "@/components/ui/skeleton"`
- Toast: `import { useToast } from "@/components/ui/toast"`

### Layout Components:
- Header: `import { Header } from "@/components/layout/header"`
- Footer: `import { Footer } from "@/components/layout/footer"`
- BottomNav: `import { BottomNav } from "@/components/layout/bottom-nav"`

## Responsive Design (Mobile-First)

### Required: Mobile-First approach
Write base styles for mobile, then expand to larger screens.

```tsx
// ✅ Correct (Mobile-First)
className="
  w-full          // mobile: full width
  md:w-1/2        // tablet: half
  lg:w-1/3        // desktop: third
"

// ❌ Wrong (Desktop-First)
className="w-1/3 md:w-1/2 sm:w-full"
```

### Breakpoints
- Default: mobile (< 768px)
- md: 768px+ (tablet)
- lg: 1024px+ (desktop)

### Class Order
Always write: base → md → lg → xl

## Touch Targets

Minimum 44x44px for all interactive elements:

```tsx
// Icon buttons
<button className="min-h-11 min-w-11 flex items-center justify-center">
  <Icon className="h-5 w-5" />
</button>

// Navigation links
<Link className="block px-4 py-3 min-h-11">Menu</Link>
```

## UI State Patterns

Every data-fetching UI must handle 4 states:

```tsx
// 1. Loading
if (isLoading) return <Skeleton className="h-32 w-full" />

// 2. Error
if (error) return (
  <div className="text-center p-8">
    <p className="text-destructive">{error.message}</p>
    <Button onClick={refetch} variant="outline" className="mt-4">
      다시 시도
    </Button>
  </div>
)

// 3. Empty
if (!data?.length) return (
  <div className="text-center p-8 text-muted-foreground">
    <p>데이터가 없습니다</p>
  </div>
)

// 4. Success
return <DataList items={data} />
```

## Form Patterns

Use controlled components with proper validation:

```tsx
const [email, setEmail] = useState('')
const [error, setError] = useState('')

const handleSubmit = (e: FormEvent) => {
  e.preventDefault()
  if (!email.includes('@')) {
    setError('유효한 이메일을 입력하세요')
    return
  }
  // Submit logic
}

<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
  <Input
    type="email"
    value={email}
    onChange={(e) => setEmail(e.target.value)}
    placeholder="email@example.com"
  />
  {error && <p className="text-sm text-destructive mt-1">{error}</p>}
  <Button type="submit">제출</Button>
</form>
```

### Validation Messages (Korean)
- Required: "필수 항목입니다"
- Email: "유효한 이메일을 입력하세요"
- Min length: "{n}자 이상 입력하세요"
- Password: "비밀번호는 8자 이상이어야 합니다"

## Never Do

- ❌ Inline styles (`style={{}}`)
- ❌ Hardcoded colors (`#007bff`, `rgb()`)
- ❌ Create new components without checking existing ones
- ❌ Desktop-First styling
- ❌ Touch targets smaller than 44px
- ❌ Skip loading/error/empty states
- ❌ Direct DOM manipulation
- ❌ Use `any` type

## Common Patterns

### Loading Skeleton
```tsx
<div className="space-y-4">
  <Skeleton className="h-8 w-48" />     {/* Title */}
  <Skeleton className="h-4 w-full" />   {/* Line 1 */}
  <Skeleton className="h-4 w-3/4" />    {/* Line 2 */}
</div>
```

### Empty State
```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-8 text-center">
  <BookOpen className="h-12 w-12 text-muted-foreground mb-4" />
  <h3 className="font-semibold">소설이 없습니다</h3>
  <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1">
    새 소설을 추가해보세요
  </p>
  <Button className="mt-4">소설 추가</Button>
</div>
```

### Responsive Grid
```tsx
<div className="grid gap-4 grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4">
  {items.map(item => <Card key={item.id} />)}
</div>
```

### Container
```tsx
<div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8">
  {children}
</div>
```
